.TH CLIAMP 1 "2026" "cliamp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cliamp \- retro terminal music player inspired by Winamp 2.x
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cliamp
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIURL\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cliamp
is a terminal music player with a Winamp\-inspired interface: a playlist
editor, a graphic equaliser, dozens of visualisers and a large collection of
themes, all rendered in the terminal.
.PP
It plays local files (MP3, FLAC, OGG, WAV) and internet radio, and can stream
from Spotify, Qobuz, Navidrome, Jellyfin, Emby, Plex, SoundCloud, NetEase and
YouTube Music.
.PP
Run without arguments to start the interactive TUI. Run with a command to
control an already running instance over its IPC socket, which makes cliamp
scriptable from status bars such as Waybar.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-vol \fIfloat\fR
Startup volume in dB, within [\-30, +6] (default: 0).
.TP
.B \-\-shuffle
Shuffle playback.
.TP
.B \-\-repeat \fImode\fR
Repeat mode: \fBoff\fR, \fBall\fR or \fBone\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-mono\fR, \fB\-\-no\-mono
Enable or disable mono output.
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-play
Start playback immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Compact mode (80 columns).
.TP
.B \-\-provider \fIname\fR
Default provider: radio, navidrome, plex, jellyfin, emby, spotify, qobuz,
soundcloud, netease, yt, youtube, ytmusic.
.TP
.B \-\-start\-theme \fIname\fR
UI theme to start with.
.TP
.B \-\-visualizer \fImode\fR
Visualizer mode.
.TP
.B \-\-eq\-preset \fIname\fR
Equaliser preset name.
.TP
.B \-\-sample\-rate \fIhz\fR
Output sample rate in Hz (0 = auto).
.TP
.B \-\-buffer\-ms \fIms\fR
Speaker buffer in milliseconds (50\-5000).
.TP
.B \-\-resample\-quality \fIn\fR
Resample quality factor (1\-4).
.TP
.B \-\-bit\-depth \fIn\fR
PCM bit depth: 16 or 32.
.TP
.B \-\-audio\-device \fIname\fR
Audio output device; use \fBlist\fR to show the available devices.
.TP
.B \-\-playlist \fIname\fR
Load a local TOML playlist by name and start playing.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level \fIlevel\fR
Log level: debug, info, warn, error.
.TP
.B \-\-expand\-playlist\fR, \fB\-\-no\-expand\-playlist
Enable or disable expansion of YouTube Music playlists from list= URLs.
.TP
.B \-\-low\-power
Low\-power mode: reduce CPU usage by lowering the UI cadence and disabling
visualisation.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon\fR, \fB\-d
Run headless (no TUI), serving IPC for scripts and status bars.
.TP
.B \-\-help\fR, \fB\-h
Show help.
.TP
.B \-\-version\fR, \fB\-v
Print the version.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Playback control
.TP
.B play\fR, \fBpause\fR, \fBtoggle\fR, \fBstop
Resume, pause, toggle or stop playback.
.TP
.B next\fR, \fBprev
Skip to the next or previous track.
.TP
.B status
Show the current playback state.
.TP
.B volume \fIdB\fR
Adjust the volume in dB.
.TP
.B seek \fIseconds\fR
Seek to a position in seconds.
.TP
.B speed \fIfactor\fR
Set the playback speed (0.25\-2.0).
.TP
.B shuffle\fR, \fBrepeat\fR, \fBmono
Toggle or set shuffle, repeat mode and mono output.
.TP
.B eq \fIpreset\fR|\fIband value\fR
Set an equaliser preset or an individual band.
.TP
.B device \fIname\fR
Switch the audio output device.
.SS Library and queue
.TP
.B load \fIplaylist\fR
Load a playlist into the player.
.TP
.B queue \fItrack\fR
Queue a track for playback.
.TP
.B playlist
Manage local playlists.
.TP
.B history
Show recently played tracks.
.SS Appearance
.TP
.B theme \fR[\fIname\fR]
Set or list UI themes.
.TP
.B vis \fR[\fImode\fR]
Set or list visualizer modes.
.TP
.B visstream
Stream visualizer bands as NDJSON, one frame per line.
.SS Integrations and maintenance
.TP
.B setup
Interactive wizard to configure remote providers.
.TP
.B spotify\fR, \fBqobuz
Manage the Spotify and Qobuz integrations.
.TP
.B plugins
Manage Lua plugins.
.TP
.B upgrade
Upgrade cliamp to the latest release. On Debian and Ubuntu, prefer
.BR apt (8)
so the package manager stays in charge of the installed files.
.TP
.B help\fR, \fBh
Show a list of commands, or help for one command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cliamp/config.toml
User configuration file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the location of the configuration directory.
